# ============================================================
#  Detections — Scheduled Alerts
#  Naming convention:  <Category> - <MITRE ATT&CK ID> - <Activity>
# ============================================================

# ---- WALKTHROUGH ALERT -------------------------------------
# Title       : Network- T1078- Successful SSH Authentication
# Description : Detect successful SSH authentication toward our SSH server.
#               Use OSINT to obtain further context on the source IP and
#               review what other activity the user performed. Pivot +/- 5
#               minutes around the event looking for indicators.
# MITRE       : T1078 (Valid Accounts)
# Permissions : Shared in App
# Schedule    : Run on Cron Schedule -> */15 * * * *   (every 15 minutes)
# Trigger     : Number of Results is greater than 0
# Action      : Add to Triggered Alerts | Severity: Medium
index="mydfir-lab1" host=linuxvm source="auth.log" sourcetype=linux_auth_logs msg="Accepted password"
| iplocation src_ip
| stats count by _time,user,Country,src_ip

# ---- SCENARIO ALERT ----------------------------------------
# Prompt      : SOC manager wants a MEDIUM severity alert that fires when a
#               new user account is created, running hourly, routed to the
#               Triggered Alerts page.
# Title       : Endpoint-T1136- New User Account Created
# Description : Detects a newly created user account. Review both activities
#               performed by the newly created user and source user for
#               potential compromise.
# MITRE       : T1136 (Create Account)
# Permissions : Shared in App
# Schedule    : Run every hour, at 0 minutes past the hour
# Trigger     : Number of Results is greater than 0
# Action      : Add to Triggered Alerts | Severity: Medium
index="mydfir-lab1" host=winvm EventCode=4720 user!=SYSTEM user!=*$
| stats count by _time,ComputerName,Subject_Account_Name,New_Account_Account_Name
